    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean i get the \"live in the moment\" thing but it feels so fake. like, a single moment doesn't change the fact that the math is all pointing to nothingness. if the final state of everything is just zero, then all this individual struggle, all the pain and the work we do to keep going... it's just inefficient. it feels like we're just delaying the inevitable and making it harder on ourselves for no reason. doesn't it seem more logical to just accept the entropy rather than trying to fight it every single day?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
