      "content": "but that \"defiance\" you're talking about just sounds like a lot of unnecessary suffering. if the energy we use to stay alive and keep fighting just gets dissipated into nothingness eventually anyway, why do we have to go through the pain part? if the outcome is the same, wouldn't it be more efficient to just reach that state of equilibrium sooner? like, instead of a long, slow descent into disorder, why not just skip to the end?",
